{
  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that multiprofile aggregation (avgpool) with scgpt boosts RNA-only accuracy from 0.411 (config_038) to 0.530 (config_011), a +0.119 gain. Meanwhile, multimodal singleprofile (config_009, 0.421) barely exceeds RNA singleprofile (0.411), suggesting resnet50 image adds little in the singleprofile regime. The critical open question is whether the multiprofile benefit transfers to the multimodal setting and whether image becomes more useful when RNA is better aggregated. config_019 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) is the minimal, single-variable extension: it adds multiprofile+avgpool to config_009 and adds resnet50+weighted to config_011, keeping all other choices (scgpt, resnet50, weighted) identical to prior runs. This cleanly isolates the interaction between multiprofile aggregation and image fusion, telling us whether to invest further in multimodal multiprofile or focus on RNA-side improvements. Under a tight budget, this one experiment resolves the most important design uncertainty."
}

